# Python via uv

This project is managed with [uv](https://docs.astral.sh/uv/). **Never** use bare `python`, `pip`, or `pytest` — always go through uv so the correct interpreter and venv are used.

## Commands

| Task | Use | Avoid |
|------|-----|-------|
| Install/sync deps | `uv sync` | `pip install`, `pip install -r requirements.txt` |
| Run a script or module | `uv run python script.py` | `python script.py` |
| Run pytest | `uv run test tests/` or `uv run pytest tests/` | `pytest tests/` |
| Run project scripts | `uv run test`, `uv run ensure-cloak`, `uv run allure-report` | invoking helpers directly without uv |
| Add a dependency | `uv add <package>` | `pip install <package>` |
| One-off tool | `uv run <tool> <args>` | installing globally or outside the project env |

## Examples

```bash
# ✅ GOOD
uv sync
uv run test tests/test_1_sign_up.py
uv run pytest tests/ -k "signup" -v
uv run python -c "from helpers.auth_excel import cell_value"

# ❌ BAD
python -m pytest tests/
pip install selenium
pytest tests/
```

## Notes

- Python version is pinned in `.python-version` (3.14); uv selects it automatically.
- On Windows (PowerShell), use `;` instead of `&&` to chain shell commands.
- Prefer documented `uv run` scripts in `pyproject.toml` (`test`, `ensure-cloak`, `allure-report`) when they fit the task.
